# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems and reduced states"
msgstr "Sisteme multiple și stări reduse"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll turn our attention to how density matrices work for multiple "
"systems, including examples of different types of correlations they can "
"express and how they can be used to describe the states of isolated parts of"
" compound systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acum ne vom îndrepta atenția spre modul în care matricele de densitate "
"funcționează pentru sisteme multiple, inclusiv exemple de diferite tipuri de"
" corelații pe care le pot exprima și cum pot fi folosite pentru a descrie "
"stările unor părți izolate din sisteme compuse.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems {#multiple-systems}"
msgstr "Sisteme multiple {#multiple-systems}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Density matrices can represent states of multiple systems in an analogous way to state vectors in the simplified formulation of quantum information, following the same basic idea that multiple systems can be viewed as if they're single, compound systems.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the rows and columns of density matrices representing states of multiple systems are placed in correspondence with the Cartesian product of the classical state sets of the individual systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matricele de densitate pot reprezenta stările unor sisteme multiple într-un mod analog vectorilor de stare din formularea simplificată a informației cuantice, urmând aceeași idee de bază că sistemele multiple pot fi privite ca și cum ar fi sisteme individuale compuse.\n"
"Din punct de vedere matematic, liniile și coloanele matricelor de densitate care reprezintă stările unor sisteme multiple sunt puse în corespondență cu produsul cartezian al mulțimilor de stări clasice ale sistemelor individuale.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, recall the state vector representations of the four Bell "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"De exemplu, reamintește-ți reprezentările prin vectori de stare ale celor "
"patru stări Bell.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representations of these states are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Reprezentările prin matrice de densitate ale acestor stări sunt "
"următoarele.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Product states {#product-states}"
msgstr "Stări produs {#product-states}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we had for state vectors, tensor products of density matrices represent *independence* between the states of multiple systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ is prepared in the state represented by the density matrix $\\rho$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ is independently prepared in the state represented by $\\sigma,$ then the density matrix describing the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is the tensor product $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Similar cu ceea ce am avut pentru vectorii de stare, produsele tensoriale ale matricelor de densitate reprezintă *independența* dintre stările mai multor sisteme.\n"
"De exemplu, dacă $\\mathsf{X}$ este pregătit în starea reprezentată de matricea de densitate $\\rho$ și $\\mathsf{Y}$ este pregătit independent în starea reprezentată de $\\sigma,$ atunci matricea de densitate care descrie starea lui $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ este produsul tensorial $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same terminology is used here as in the simplified formulation of "
"quantum information: states of this form are referred to as *product "
"states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aceeași terminologie este folosită aici ca în formularea simplificată a "
"informației cuantice: stările de această formă sunt denumite *stări "
"produs*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correlated and entangled states {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"
msgstr "Stări corelate și entanglate {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States that cannot be expressed as product states represent *correlations* between systems.\n"
"There are, in fact, different types of correlations that can be represented by density matrices.\n"
"Here are a few examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Stările care nu pot fi exprimate ca stări produs reprezintă *corelații* între sisteme.\n"
"Există, de fapt, diferite tipuri de corelații care pot fi reprezentate prin matrice de densitate.\n"
"Iată câteva exemple.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Correlated classical states.*\n"
"For example, we can express the situation in which Alice and Bob share a random bit like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Stări clasice corelate.*\n"
"De exemplu, putem exprima situația în care Alice și Bob împart un bit aleator astfel:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Ensembles of quantum states.*\n"
"Suppose we have $m$ density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ all representing states of a system $\\mathsf{X},$ and we  randomly choose one of these states according to a probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Such a process is represented by an *ensemble* of states, which includes the specification of the density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ as well as the probabilities $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ We can associate an ensemble of states with a single density matrix, describing both the random choice of $k$ and the corresponding density matrix $\\rho_k,$ like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ansambluri de stări cuantice.*\n"
"Să presupunem că avem $m$ matrice de densitate $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ toate reprezentând stări ale unui sistem $\\mathsf{X},$ și alegem aleator una dintre aceste stări conform unui vector de probabilitate $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Un astfel de proces este reprezentat de un *ansamblu* de stări, care include specificarea matricelor de densitate $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ precum și probabilitățile $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Putem asocia un ansamblu de stări cu o singură matrice de densitate, descriind atât alegerea aleatoare a lui $k$, cât și matricea de densitate corespunzătoare $\\rho_k,$ astfel:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To be clear, this is the state of a pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ "
"where $\\mathsf{Y}$ represents the classical selection of $k$ — so we're "
"assuming its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ States of this "
"form are sometimes called *classical-quantum states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Pentru a fi clar, aceasta este starea unei perechi "
"$(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ unde $\\mathsf{Y}$ reprezintă selecția clasică a"
" lui $k$ — deci presupunem că mulțimea sa de stări clasice este "
"$\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ Stările de această formă sunt uneori numite *stări "
"clasic-cuantice*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Separable states*. We can imagine situations in which we have a classical "
"correlation among the quantum states of two systems like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Stări separabile*. Ne putem imagina situații în care avem o corelație "
"clasică între stările cuantice ale două sisteme, astfel:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In words, for each $k$ from $0$ to $m-1,$ we have that with probability "
"$p_k$ the system on the left is in the state $\\rho_k$ and the system on the"
" right is in the state $\\sigma_k.$ States like this are called *separable "
"states*. This concept can also be extended to more than two systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
"   Cu alte cuvinte, pentru fiecare $k$ de la $0$ la $m-1,$ avem că cu probabilitatea $p_k$ sistemul din stânga se află în starea $\\rho_k$ și sistemul din dreapta se află în starea $\\sigma_k.$ Stările de acest tip se numesc *stări separabile*. Acest concept poate fi extins și la mai mult de două sisteme.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Entangled states*. Not all states of pairs of systems are separable. In the"
" general formulation of quantum information, this is how entanglement is "
"defined: states that are not separable are said to be *entangled*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Stări entanglate*. Nu toate stările perechilor de sisteme sunt separabile. "
"În formularea generală a informației cuantice, astfel este definit "
"entanglementul: stările care nu sunt separabile sunt numite *entanglate*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that this terminology is consistent with the terminology we used in "
"the \"Basics of quantum information\" course. There we said that quantum "
"state vectors that are not product states represent entangled states — and "
"indeed, for any quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that is not a "
"product state, we find that the state represented by the density matrix "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is not separable. Entanglement is "
"much more complicated than this for states that are not pure.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Reține că această terminologie este consecventă cu terminologia folosită "
"în cursul „Bazele informației cuantice\". Acolo am spus că vectorii de stare"
" cuantică care nu sunt stări produs reprezintă stări entanglate — și într-"
"adevăr, pentru orice vector de stare cuantică $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ care nu "
"este o stare produs, constatăm că starea reprezentată de matricea de "
"densitate $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ nu este separabilă. "
"Entanglementul este mult mai complicat decât atât pentru stările care nu "
"sunt pure.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states and the partial trace {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"
msgstr "Stări reduse și urma parțială {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a simple but important thing we can do with density matrices in the context of multiple systems, which is to describe the states we obtain by ignoring some of the systems.\n"
"When multiple systems are in a quantum state and we discard or choose to ignore one or more of the systems,\n"
"the state of the remaining systems is called the *reduced state* of those systems.\n"
"Density matrix descriptions of reduced states are easily obtained through a mapping, known as the *partial trace*, from the density matrix describing the state of the whole.\n"
msgstr ""
"Există ceva simplu, dar important pe care îl putem face cu matricele de densitate în contextul sistemelor multiple, și anume să descriem stările pe care le obținem ignorând unele dintre sisteme.\n"
"Când mai multe sisteme se află într-o stare cuantică și eliminăm sau alegem să ignorăm unul sau mai multe sisteme,\n"
"starea sistemelor rămase se numește *starea redusă* a acelor sisteme.\n"
"Descrierile prin matrice de densitate ale stărilor reduse se obțin cu ușurință printr-o aplicație, cunoscută sub numele de *urmă parțială*, din matricea de densitate care descrie starea întregului.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: reduced states for an e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"
msgstr ""
"Exemplu: stări reduse pentru un e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ that are "
"together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Să presupunem că avem o pereche de qubiți $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ care "
"se află împreună în starea\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can imagine that Alice holds the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ and Bob holds $\\mathsf{B},$ which is to say that together they share an e-bit.\n"
"We'd like to have a density matrix description of Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, as if Bob decided to take his qubit and visit the stars, never to be seen again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ne putem imagina că Alice deține qubitul $\\mathsf{A}$ și Bob deține $\\mathsf{B},$ cu alte cuvinte, împreună ei împart un e-bit.\n"
"Am dori să avem o descriere prin matrice de densitate a qubitului $\\mathsf{A}$ al lui Alice în izolare, ca și cum Bob ar fi decis să-și ia qubitul și să viziteze stelele, fără să mai fie văzut vreodată.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First let's think about what would happen if Bob decided somewhere on his journey to measure his qubit with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"If he did this, he would obtain the outcome $0$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Mai întâi, să ne gândim ce s-ar întâmpla dacă Bob ar decide, undeva pe parcursul călătoriei sale, să măsoare qubitul cu o măsurătoare în baza standard.\n"
"Dacă ar face acest lucru, ar obține rezultatul $0$ cu probabilitatea\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ and he "
"would obtain the outcome $1$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"caz în care starea qubitului lui Alice devine $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ și ar "
"obține rezultatul $1$ cu probabilitatea\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "caz în care starea qubitului lui Alice devine $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we ignore Bob's measurement outcome and focus on Alice's qubit, we conclude that she obtains the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ with probability $1/2.$\n"
"This leads us to describe the state of Alice's qubit in isolation by the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Deci, dacă ignorăm rezultatul măsurătorii lui Bob și ne concentrăm pe qubitul lui Alice, concluzionăm că ea obține starea $\\vert 0\\rangle$ cu probabilitatea $1/2$ și starea $\\vert 1\\rangle$ cu probabilitatea $1/2.$\n"
"Aceasta ne conduce să descriem starea qubitului lui Alice în izolare prin matricea de densitate\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, Alice's qubit is in the completely mixed state.\n"
"To be clear, this description of the state of Alice's qubit doesn't include Bob's measurement outcome; we're ignoring Bob altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"Adică, qubitul lui Alice se află în starea complet mixtă.\n"
"Pentru a fi clar, această descriere a stării qubitului lui Alice nu include rezultatul măsurătorii lui Bob; îl ignorăm complet pe Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it might seem like the density matrix description of Alice's qubit in isolation that we've just obtained relies on the assumption that Bob has measured his qubit, but this is not actually so.\n"
"What we've done is to use the possibility that Bob measures his qubit to argue that the completely mixed state arises as the state of Alice's qubit, based on what we've already learned.\n"
"Of course, nothing says that Bob must measure his qubit — but nothing says that he doesn't.\n"
"And if he's light years away, then nothing he does or doesn't do can possibly influence the state of Alice's qubit viewed it in isolation.\n"
"That is to say, the description we've obtained for the state of Alice's qubit is the only description consistent with the impossibility of faster-than-light communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acum, s-ar părea că descrierea prin matrice de densitate a qubitului lui Alice în izolare pe care tocmai am obținut-o depinde de presupunerea că Bob și-a măsurat qubitul, dar de fapt nu este așa.\n"
"Ceea ce am făcut este să folosim posibilitatea că Bob își măsoară qubitul pentru a argumenta că starea complet mixtă apare ca stare a qubitului lui Alice, pe baza a ceea ce am învățat deja.\n"
"Desigur, nimic nu spune că Bob trebuie să-și măsoare qubitul — dar nimic nu spune că nu o face.\n"
"Și dacă se află la ani-lumină distanță, atunci nimic din ceea ce face sau nu face nu poate influența starea qubitului lui Alice văzut în izolare.\n"
"Cu alte cuvinte, descrierea pe care am obținut-o pentru starea qubitului lui Alice este singura descriere compatibilă cu imposibilitatea comunicării mai rapide decât lumina.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also consider the state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ which happens to be the completely mixed state as well.\n"
"Indeed, for all four Bell states we find that the reduced state of both Alice's qubit and Bob's qubit is the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Putem considera și starea qubitului $\\mathsf{B}$ al lui Bob, care se întâmplă să fie de asemenea starea complet mixtă.\n"
"Într-adevăr, pentru toate cele patru stări Bell constatăm că starea redusă atât a qubitului lui Alice, cât și a qubitului lui Bob este starea complet mixtă.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states for a general quantum state vector {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"
msgstr ""
"Stări reduse pentru un vector de stare cuantică general {#reduced-states-"
"for-a-general-quantum-state-vector}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's generalize the example just discussed to two arbitrary systems $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B},$ not necessarily qubits in the state $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"We'll assume the classical state sets of $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are $\\Sigma$ and $\\Gamma,$ respectively.\n"
"A density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the combined system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ therefore has row and column indices corresponding to the Cartesian product $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Acum să generalizăm exemplul tocmai discutat la două sisteme arbitrare $\\mathsf{A}$ și $\\mathsf{B},$ nu neapărat qubiți în starea $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Vom presupune că mulțimile de stări clasice ale lui $\\mathsf{A}$ și $\\mathsf{B}$ sunt $\\Sigma$ și, respectiv, $\\Gamma.$\n"
"O matrice de densitate $\\rho$ care reprezintă o stare a sistemului combinat $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ are deci indici de linie și coloană corespunzători produsului cartezian $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that the state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is described by the quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ so the density matrix describing this state is $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"We'll obtain a density matrix description of the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, which is conventionally denoted $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(A superscript is also sometimes used rather than a subscript.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Să presupunem că starea lui $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ este descrisă de vectorul de stare cuantică $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ astfel încât matricea de densitate care descrie această stare este $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"Vom obține o descriere prin matrice de densitate a stării lui $\\mathsf{A}$ în izolare, care este notată în mod convențional $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(Uneori se folosește un superscript în loc de subscript.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ can be expressed in the form\n"
msgstr "Vectorul de stare $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ poate fi exprimat în forma\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a uniquely determined collection of vectors $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}.$\n"
"In particular, these vectors can be determined through a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"pentru o colecție de vectori $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}$ determinată în mod unic.\n"
"În particular, acești vectori pot fi determinați printr-o formulă simplă.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reasoning similarly to the previous example of an e-bit, if we were to "
"measure the system $\\mathsf{B}$ with a standard basis measurement, we would"
" obtain each outcome $b\\in\\Gamma$ with probability "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ in which case the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Raționând similar cu exemplul anterior al unui e-bit, dacă am măsura "
"sistemul $\\mathsf{B}$ cu o măsurătoare în baza standard, am obține fiecare "
"rezultat $b\\in\\Gamma$ cu probabilitatea $\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ "
"caz în care starea lui $\\mathsf{A}$ devine\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As a density matrix, this state can be written as follows.\n"
msgstr "Ca matrice de densitate, această stare poate fi scrisă astfel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Averaging the different states according to the probabilities of the "
"respective outcomes, we arrive at the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Făcând media diferitelor stări conform probabilităților rezultatelor "
"respective, ajungem la matricea de densitate\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace {#the-partial-trace}"
msgstr "Urma parțială {#the-partial-trace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The formula\n"
msgstr "Formula\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"leads us to the description of the reduced state of $\\mathsf{A}$ for any "
"density matrix $\\rho$ of the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ not just a "
"pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"ne conduce la descrierea stării reduse a lui $\\mathsf{A}$ pentru orice "
"matrice de densitate $\\rho$ a perechii $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ nu doar"
" pentru o stare pură.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula must work, simply by linearity together with the fact that "
"every density matrix can be written as a convex combination of pure "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Această formulă trebuie să funcționeze, pur și simplu prin liniaritate "
"împreună cu faptul că orice matrice de densitate poate fi scrisă ca o "
"combinație convexă de stări pure.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation being performed on $\\rho$ to obtain $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ in this equation is known as the *partial trace*, and to be more precise we say that the partial trace is performed on $\\mathsf{B},$ or that $\\mathsf{B}$ is *traced out*.\n"
"This operation is denoted $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ so we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Operația efectuată asupra lui $\\rho$ pentru a obține $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ în această ecuație este cunoscută sub numele de *urmă parțială*, și mai precis spunem că urma parțială se efectuează pe $\\mathsf{B},$ sau că $\\mathsf{B}$ este *eliminat prin urmă*.\n"
"Această operație este notată $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ deci putem scrie\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also define the partial trace on $\\mathsf{A},$ so it's the system "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ that gets traced out rather than $\\mathsf{B},$ like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Putem defini de asemenea urma parțială pe $\\mathsf{A},$ astfel încât "
"sistemul $\\mathsf{A}$ este cel eliminat prin urmă, nu $\\mathsf{B},$ "
"astfel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives us the density matrix description $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ of the "
"state of $\\mathsf{B}$ in isolation rather than $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Aceasta ne dă descrierea prin matrice de densitate $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ a "
"stării lui $\\mathsf{B}$ în izolare, în loc de $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To recapitulate, if $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is any pair of systems and "
"we have a density matrix $\\rho$ describing a state of "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ the *reduced states* of the systems "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pentru a recapitula, dacă $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ este orice pereche de "
"sisteme și avem o matrice de densitate $\\rho$ care descrie o stare a lui "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ *stările reduse* ale sistemelor $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"și $\\mathsf{B}$ sunt următoarele.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho$ is a density matrix, then $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ will also necessarily be density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dacă $\\rho$ este o matrice de densitate, atunci $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ și "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ vor fi în mod necesar tot matrice de densitate.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These notions can be generalized to any number of systems in place of two in a natural way.\n"
"In general, we can put the names of whatever systems we choose in the subscript of a density matrix $\\rho$ to describe the reduced state of just those systems.\n"
"For example, if $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ and $\\mathsf{C}$ are systems and $\\rho$ is a density matrix describing a state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ then we can define\n"
msgstr ""
"Aceste noțiuni pot fi generalizate la orice număr de sisteme în loc de două, într-un mod natural.\n"
"În general, putem pune numele oricăror sisteme la alegere în subscriptul unei matrice de densitate $\\rho$ pentru a descrie starea redusă doar a acelor sisteme.\n"
"De exemplu, dacă $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B}$ și $\\mathsf{C}$ sunt sisteme și $\\rho$ este o matrice de densitate care descrie o stare a lui $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ atunci putem defini\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and similarly for other choices for the systems.\n"
msgstr "și similar pentru alte alegeri ale sistemelor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternative description of the partial trace {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Descriere alternativă a urmei parțiale {#alternative-description-of-the-"
"partial-trace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to describe the partial trace mappings "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ is"
" that they are the *unique* linear mappings that satisfy the formulas\n"
msgstr ""
"O modalitate alternativă de a descrie aplicațiile urmei parțiale "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ și $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ "
"este că acestea sunt aplicațiile liniare *unice* care satisfac formulele\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these formulas, $N$ and $M$ are square matrices of the appropriate sizes:\n"
"the rows and columns of $M$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{A}$ and the rows and columns of $N$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"În aceste formule, $N$ și $M$ sunt matrice pătrate de dimensiunile corespunzătoare:\n"
"liniile și coloanele lui $M$ corespund stărilor clasice ale lui $\\mathsf{A}$, iar liniile și coloanele lui $N$ corespund stărilor clasice ale lui $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This characterization of the partial trace is not only fundamental from a mathematical viewpoint, but can also allow for quick calculations in some situations.\n"
"For example, consider this state of a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Această caracterizare a urmei parțiale nu este doar fundamentală din punct de vedere matematic, ci poate permite și calcule rapide în anumite situații.\n"
"De exemplu, consideră această stare a unei perechi de qubiți $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To compute the reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ for instance, we can use linearity together with the fact that\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ and $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ have unit trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pentru a calcula starea redusă $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$, de exemplu, putem folosi liniaritatea împreună cu faptul că\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ și $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ au urmă unitară.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ can be computed similarly.\n"
msgstr "Starea redusă $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ poate fi calculată similar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace for two qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"
msgstr "Urma parțială pentru doi qubiți {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partial trace can also be described explicitly in terms of matrices.\n"
"Here we'll do this just for two qubits, but this can also be generalized to larger systems.\n"
"Assume that we have two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ so that any density matrix describing a state of these two qubits can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"Urma parțială poate fi descrisă explicit și în termeni de matrice.\n"
"Aici vom face acest lucru doar pentru doi qubiți, dar aceasta poate fi generalizată și pentru sisteme mai mari.\n"
"Să presupunem că avem doi qubiți $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ astfel încât orice matrice de densitate care descrie o stare a acestor doi qubiți poate fi scrisă ca\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some choice of complex numbers $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"pentru o alegere oarecare de numere complexe $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq "
"j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace over the first system has the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Urma parțială peste primul sistem are următoarea formulă.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to think about this formula begins by viewing $4\\times 4$ matrices as $2\\times 2$ block matrices, where each block is $2\\times 2.$\n"
"That is,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"O modalitate de a înțelege această formulă pornește de la vizualizarea matricelor $4\\times 4$ ca matrice bloc $2\\times 2,$ unde fiecare bloc este $2\\times 2.$\n"
"Adică,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "pentru\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then have\n"
msgstr "Avem atunci\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the formula when the second system is traced out rather than the "
"first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iată formula când al doilea sistem este eliminat prin urmă în loc de "
"primul.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"În termeni de matrice bloc de o formă similară cu cea anterioară, avem această formulă.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In terms of block matrices of a form similar to before, we have this "
"formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Descrierile prin matrice bloc ale acestor funcții pot fi extinse la sisteme "
"mai mari decât qubiții într-un mod natural și direct.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The block matrix descriptions of these functions can be extended to systems "
"larger than qubits in a natural and direct way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pentru a încheia lecția, să aplicăm aceste formule la aceeași stare "
"considerată mai sus.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To finish the lesson, let's apply these formulas to the same state we "
"considered above.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr "Starea redusă a primului sistem $\\mathsf{A}$ este\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state of the first system $\\mathsf{A}$ is\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr "și starea redusă a celui de-al doilea sistem $\\mathsf{B}$ este\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the reduced state of the second system $\\mathsf{B}$ is\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
